{
	"_note": "The village, rebuilt 2026-11-14 after the user's map of Arashiyama (v2, 56 x 48; the old one is git tag town-classic): the river in from the gorge at the west edge, bending east along the south, with a riverside road on its north bank and a long wooden bridge (x 40-42) to the park on the south bank and on to Minamino (south edge). The stone main street (x 40-42) runs north from the bridge to the Sagano line (y 2) and Kaminoda (north edge). West of it the temple (Tenryu-ji in spirit) inside its earthen wall: the gate on the street (34, 21-22), the hall, the kitchen hall, the garden pond (the village's fishing water, data/fish.json), a north gate to the bamboo path; shops facing the street (street: east) and Kota's family's house by the river (door 37, 33) with the carp streamers' socket beside it; the art museum by the river. North the bamboo path (y 11-12) through thick bamboo, the little shrine (Nonomiya in spirit) with its black torii, Ogura pond on its path west, the lane up to the farm (north edge, x 34-35), the small station on the line in the north-west; the hill's pines and maples west. East along alleys: Grandma Tome's house (door 46, 8), the post office (door 51, 8; Ren lives there), the Kurogane Smithy (door 44, 15; Hachiro), the Hinata Clinic (door 51, 15; Dr. Yae; a collapse wakes the farmer there), the station with its line east, the Yorozu Store (door 46, 28) with Sayo's side door (48, 28), a shop, and the road east to Sakurazaka (y 29-30). Doors open by their `hours` and say `closed` otherwise. The two store_sign props are the store's new sign (flag sayo_sign, old / new, heart_sayo_5). Format: README.md, Maps.",
